.TH UTIMES 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
utimes \- Linux x86-64 syscall 235
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B int utimes(const char* path, const struct timeval* times);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Sets file access and modification times.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR utimes (2)
